    ],
    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 11,
        "sourceEnd": 165,
        "text": "Okay, everyone, thanks for coming. We have forty minutes to agree on what the pilot data actually supports. Let's start with the attendance figures. Ravi?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "490b94d0025b52abed48895fce5d85cd87d64f3b29cbb694b0365449be508257",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ravi patel",
        "speaker": "Ravi Patel",
        "sourceStart": 179,
        "sourceEnd": 624,
        "text": "Sure. Across the twelve-week pilot, average attendance in the three intervention schools rose from 71 percent to 79 percent. In the two comparison schools, it stayed flat at about 72 percent. So the direction is encouraging. But I want to be careful: the comparison schools were not randomly chosen, and they are smaller. That means any difference could be due to factors other than the program itself, such as school size or student background.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "23f773ddc1b8229d6cc698c040c27c8c91a371713f7217e08961f100e2736a36",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 637,
        "sourceEnd": 761,
        "text": "Right. So we can say attendance improved in the intervention schools, but we cannot say the program caused it. Is that fair?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "aaf9aec4f9a233a30df519991bca5879bbb2e7c571fc2b8aea2edaf93fd205ea",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ravi patel",
        "speaker": "Ravi Patel",
        "sourceStart": 775,
        "sourceEnd": 964,
        "text": "That's fair. Also, one intervention school had a flu outbreak in week nine. That probably pushed its numbers down, not up. So the true effect might be slightly larger, but we can't be sure.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "87451d9d7159035f97d8d2999f7fe1d1ace1bd487e8795c24d7e6b41d7ebc728",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena ortiz",
        "speaker": "Lena Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 978,
        "sourceEnd": 1299,
        "text": "Can I add the survey results? We had 214 student responses. Sixty-two percent said they felt more confident speaking in class. But the response rate was only 48 percent, so the students who answered may not represent everyone. Those who feel more confident might be more likely to respond, which could inflate the figure.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "11d65a14ecb82b24fa11f54b37aee827f249957a59208f51b9deac5e7588be31",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1312,
        "sourceEnd": 1402,
        "text": "Good point. So we report the figure with the response rate next to it. No sweeping claims.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ec1ac8fe0b7956494a62e39c3149a0c1d5c1c8ce4c505567582bf46a562ffa0d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ravi patel",
        "speaker": "Ravi Patel",
        "sourceStart": 1416,
        "sourceEnd": 1627,
        "text": "Agreed. And on teacher workload, the logs show an average of 3.2 extra hours per week in the first month, falling to 1.4 hours by week ten. That suggests the workload eased as teachers got used to the materials.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "6a0b6ce779e630e442471b9f7222bd01b5534b2cfee6bfef1da94e0156dd1f28",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena ortiz",
        "speaker": "Lena Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 1641,
        "sourceEnd": 1869,
        "text": "Or it suggests some teachers stopped logging carefully. We should check the completion rate of the logs before we lean on that trend. If completion dropped, the later average might be based on fewer, perhaps less busy, teachers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "dfb1de0a0fea81bea9eca33c57f5816a88f56cf684bdd0756a92f49f599f901a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1882,
        "sourceEnd": 2010,
        "text": "Noted. Let's put that as a limitation. Now, the writing scores. The mean gain was 0.4 on our internal scale. Is that meaningful?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "1805b7b789ca7f943a81fbd08367695c27be6eaefeedfda19e4ae7714ebdc385",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ravi patel",
        "speaker": "Ravi Patel",
        "sourceStart": 2024,
        "sourceEnd": 2219,
        "text": "Honestly, with this sample size, 0.4 is within the range we'd expect from normal variation. I wouldn't call it a clear improvement. We'd need a larger sample to detect a real effect of that size.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "1da75daa3c6100fba50478512e379c7f1551522fe9fbd0a7a5b3a05c78df814a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena ortiz",
        "speaker": "Lena Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 2233,
        "sourceEnd": 2356,
        "text": "I agree. I'd say 'a modest positive signal that needs confirmation.' That wording keeps the door open without overclaiming.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e1f2f0613a851833d9f03e6c305f6ed68fdacf3cf24815a084bf8b148eb7af9e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2369,
        "sourceEnd": 2594,
        "text": "Let's use that wording. So, decisions. First, we recommend continuing the program for another term. Second, we ask for a larger, randomized study before any scale-up. Third, we publish the limitations clearly. Any objections?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "cb7808129c39419f159c3cf89568415faf6610381055f22e313a90470e7e2c2f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ravi patel",
        "speaker": "Ravi Patel",
        "sourceStart": 2608,
        "sourceEnd": 2765,
        "text": "No objections. But I'd add one action: we should fix the logging form so completion is easier to track. That way, future workload data will be more reliable.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "47ea36ae089a1931c927ade53a14b49f70df346ae9e7b1e1256c8c0fa7dfb8cc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena ortiz",
        "speaker": "Lena Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 2779,
        "sourceEnd": 2892,
        "text": "Yes, and we should report the attendance figure with the flu outbreak noted. That gives readers the full context.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "91e854fa35ba7ece67849575bf815d9debe18c3e464919e2ac94496348570a7d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2905,
        "sourceEnd": 3014,
        "text": "Done. I'll draft the summary by Friday. Ravi, can you prepare the attendance table? Lena, the survey section?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "112fde4c4728ca7be6e4632e463f3e51845c7f1a40a141c841913f0a7c13a399",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ravi patel",
        "speaker": "Ravi Patel",
        "sourceStart": 3028,
        "sourceEnd": 3059,
        "text": "I can do the table by Thursday.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "91ce278b85bc7dfbd274ac47b58c928b4fa7f524141643684d556268403d39b4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena ortiz",
        "speaker": "Lena Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 3073,
        "sourceEnd": 3126,
        "text": "I'll have the survey section ready by Friday morning.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "1582c73ff8798aa1ce8d6c5221c7af2221dd056a1946df021e7ae67d053cbb0f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3139,
        "sourceEnd": 3287,
        "text": "Perfect. One last thing: in the summary, avoid the phrase 'proves the program works.' We say 'is consistent with a positive effect.' Everyone clear?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a83cce4c7605d750131bfb91bf3997453e9e64149cc342534e2b9944dc29bcfb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ravi patel",
        "speaker": "Ravi Patel",
        "sourceStart": 3301,
        "sourceEnd": 3307,
        "text": "Clear.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "0781ca99c4c91c89cf7d8bbaa79e890004c650cd01e72c29575e9d5731affc20",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena ortiz",
        "speaker": "Lena Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 3321,
        "sourceEnd": 3341,
        "text": "Clear. Thanks, Maya.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "2f1f5829a1de20fdce0503885533fa189a30b5abd452f2caaab31d0bf1c888ed",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
